# Fictional EP Tracklist

## Track 1: Seven Marks Past the Birch Cut

**Story & Context:** At 118 BPM, Austėja opens alone with a seven-attack kanklės cell: low fifth, upper octave, neighboring second, repeated fifth, upper fourth, tonic, muted return. Felix enters after two cycles with an unwavering motorik kick and dry snare. Because the seven-attack phrase does not fit the four-beat bar, its low fifth gradually appears against different drum positions. Matas holds one open-fifth organ field for sixteen bars and plays only two guitar octave markers during the entire first section. Greta waits until the first full Survey Return, then enters with one low bass-harmonica tonic exactly when the first kanklės attack and kick downbeat coincide again. The hook is not a new melody; it is the audible relief of two independent clocks meeting.

The middle section uses Sleeper Hold. Austėja stops for four bars while drums, one organ tone, and faint tambourine continue. She re-enters the same seven-attack figure on beat three rather than beat one, creating a new migration pattern without changing any notes.

